From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] radv: the objects the driver keeps are made inside a long-lived scope (eden_heap_long_lived_enter/leave), so the app's heap can keep them out of the compile threads' arenas

T175b. After heydemoura/EglantinePS5 PR 104 (branch perf/heap-memory, commit
0a5efdc, docs/HEAP-MEMORY-RESEARCH.md), which measured that after a cold
shader build the eight compile threads hold 231 arenas (462 MiB) with 83 MiB
live, the rest pinned by the driver's long-lived objects allocated between
the compiler's short-lived blocks, and proposed this as "next steps" 1 (not
written there). The code here is ours.

A scope (u_eden_long_lived_enter/leave, src/util/u_eden_long_lived.h) around:
- vk_pipeline_cache_object_deserialize: ops->deserialize, i.e. every cache
  object made (a radv_shader via radv_shader_deserialize, a pipeline cache
  object, raw data), from the disk cache, the app's data or radv_shader_create;
- radv_shader_create_uncached: the shader, its shader arena block and its host
  code copy (shader->code);
- radv_parse_binary_debug_info: the debug info kept with the shader
  (statistics, strings, debug_info);
- radv_shader_part_create: prologs and epilogs (kept in the device's caches);
- radv_pipeline_cache_object_create: the object a compiled pipeline is cached as;
- the graphics, graphics library and compute pipeline objects (vk_zalloc2),
  and the gs_compute record of a pipeline;
- radv_CreateDescriptorSetLayout: the layout (vk_descriptor_set_layout_zalloc);
- radv_CreatePipelineLayout and radv_CreateDescriptorUpdateTemplate: the
  layout and the template (EglantinePS5 makes both on its builder threads).
Nothing else: the blob a cache object is read from, the disk cache's copies
and every compiler allocation stay outside.

The two functions are the app's (EglantinePS5 headless/heap_arenas.inc),
declared weak: a program without them links and the scopes do nothing.
tools/isolate-radv.py renames defined symbols only; these are undefined in the
driver and keep their names, as eden_radv_out_of_memory (lead-mesh-22) does.
In the app they do nothing unless RADV_PS5_LONGLIVED_ARENA=1 (one relaxed load
and a return otherwise).

Nothing about shader compilation, keys, cache entries, files, the build id or
the cache UUID changes (the UUID comes from the pinned build id, see
tools/patch-radv-series.py). Anchors of tools/patch-radv-wsi.py in
radv_shader.c, radv_pipeline_cache.c and radv_pipeline_compute.c checked: each
still found once (it has none in the other files).

Applied after lead-mesh-01..41 on the pinned Mesa (f5610fe) with git apply.
Compiled in the T175b build. Not run on the console.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5
---
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_descriptor_set.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_descriptor_set.c
